judging by the grandness and length of  this wall you could be forgiven for  thinking that it's in China but this is  the Great Wall of India become bell  gutter wall is located in Moraga Stan  roughly a 10 hour drive from New Delhi  its remoteness has caused this stunning  location to be relatively unknown even  to locals the wall is made of thousands  of stone bricks with artistic flourishes  on top it has seven gateways and took  over a century to construct it was a  place of refuge in times of danger the  wall snakes through valleys and along  mountaintops after the Great Wall of  China it is the second longest  continuous wall in the world it is 22  miles in length and surrounds the fort  of over 300 Asian temples that were  believed to have been built in the 15th  century in 2013 it was declared a UNESCO  World Heritage Site a majority of the  wall sits high serving as a lookout and  giving incredible views of the  surrounding mountains and farmlands  unlike anywhere else in India
 

